            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Italian for the reform, then the Italian for the member of parliament."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: rilevante",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rilevante — \"relevant, significant\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Questo dettaglio non è rilevante. This detail is not relevant."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It also means considerable: una somma rilevante."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "rilevante is the present participle of rilevare \"to raise, to point out\", from Latin relevāre \"to lift up again\" (Lewis & Short), built on levāre \"to raise\": what stands out."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
